# Open Graph link previews

Read **`additionals/guidelines/agent-devlog-og-previews.md`** before editing the
link-preview router, its Caddy routing, or either copy of `blogSocialMeta.ts`.

**Index:** `additionals/guidelines/agent-devlog-index.md`

## Quick rules (full detail in that file)

- **Two guards, both in CI:** `pnpm test:og-routing` (Caddy `@ogPreview` ⇄ the router's
  regexes) and `pnpm test:og-contract` (the duplicated OG modules must not drift).
- **`blogSocialMeta.ts` exists twice, byte-identical** — `frontend/src/og/` and
  `backend/src/og/`. Edit one, copy it over the other. The backend's tsconfig
  `rootDir: "src"` is why there is no shared import.
- **The router is total over what Caddy sends it** — `OG_PREFIX_RE` is the catch-all
  shell branch, so a routed path can never hit the Express 404.
- **`@ogPreview` sits after the filesystem handlers and the `.html` 404**, so a real
  file or a static case-study directory is served from disk and never reaches the API.
- **Never cache an injected body.** `Vary: User-Agent` plus `max-age=0` — Cloudflare's
  cache ignores `Vary: User-Agent`, so a cached body would cross the crawler/browser line.
- **`handle_errors` keeps the error status** — the shell fallback must
  `respond "{file./srv/index.html}" 200`, and `{file.}` does not resolve against `root`.
- **Test:** `curl -A 'facebookexternalhit/1.1' -s https://www.design-bakery.com/blogs/1 | grep -o '<title>[^<]*</title>'`
